  "description": "Change of use from dwelling house (Use class C3) to 7 bed HMO for 10 persons (Sui Generis); cycle storage (Retrospective)",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Marlborough",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:18:27.137Z",
  "street_name": "HINDES ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The proposal has failed to demonstrate that it would provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers or adequately safeguard the amenity of neighbouring residents, to the detriment of their residential amenities, contrary to policies S4(2)(c), DP3 and L2(d) (ii)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policy D6 and D14 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies HO10 and GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The proposed change of use to a 7-bedroom House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) would result in an over-intensive form of development that is inappropriate within an area characterised by family housing and with only moderate public transport accessibility(PTAL3). Furthermore, the proposal would fail to provide satisfactory living conditions for future occupiers and would result in inadequate and impractical frontage, landscaping and refuse storage arrangements, causing harm to the character and appearance of the property and surrounding area and would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to policies S4(2)(c), DP3, HO7 and L2(d) (ii) of National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Criteria (2), (3), (4), (6), (8), (9) and (10) of Policy HO10 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would not be in keeping with the character of the area and would be at odds with the established predominance of single-family dwellings which characterise the area. In addition, the proposed location of bin stores and parking to the front forecourt to the quantum necessary to adequately serve the proposed development would result in visual clutter negatively impacting the character and appearance of the existing dwelling and wider street scene. The likely level of occupation would significantly increase from that of an existing single family dwellinghouse which would harm the established character of the area by virtue of increased movements, noise and disturbance and would be harmful to the residential amenities of neighbouring occupiers. The proposals are found to be contrary to policies S4(2)(c), DP3 and L2(d) (ii)&amp;nbsp; of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies D3.D (1), (11) of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, in the absence of a legal agreement to secure a car free development and failure to demonstrate parking availability in the surrounding highway network and safe access and egress of the proposed off-street vehicle car parking space, in conjunction with the proposed siting of the bin stores and boundary treatment to the application site’s frontage, would likely exacerbate on street parking pressures and result in an adverse impact on highway safety in terms of occupiers’ and visitors’ unimpeded pedestrian access to the application site and highway safety of wider pedestrian users of the footpath along Hindes Road. The proposed development is therefore contrary to policies T3 TR4 and TR6 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies D3 D. (1), (4),&amp;nbsp; (11) and Policy T4(f) of the London Plan (2021) and Policies GR1, M1, M2 and CE1(B) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
